<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Legacy (API 26-30) Auto-Backup rules. Owner decision 2026-08-23: no LogEZ data is eligible
    for Google's cloud Auto-Backup transport — the manual zip backup (Settings > Data) is the
    sole off-device copy.

    Every domain is excluded EXPLICITLY. An earlier version of this file was empty on the belief
    that "not listing a path yields zero data backed up" — that is backwards. With no <include>
    element, full-backup-content backs up the DEFAULT set (databases, shared_prefs, files, and
    the app's root), and <exclude> only subtracts from it. An empty file therefore backed up all
    of the user's data to the cloud on every pre-31 device, which is the opposite of the
    decision above. (data_extraction_rules.xml already states the correct rule for API 31+.)

    Pre-31 Android has no cloud-vs-device-transfer distinction, so excluding everything here also
    disables device-to-device transfer on those versions; that is the accepted cost of the
    no-cloud posture, and the zip backup covers the move.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="root" path="." />
    <exclude domain="file" path="." />
    <exclude domain="database" path="." />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
    <exclude domain="external" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
